<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan unemployment rate unchanged at 3.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan unemployment rate unchanged at 3.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's seasonally adjusted unemployment rate in January remained unchanged from December at 3.3 percent, while the closely watched jobs-to-applicants ratio was also unchanged at 0.76, the government announced on Friday.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the jobs data:</p>
<p> (Adjusted)			  January   December  Year ago</p>
<p> Unemployment rate		  3.3 pct   3.3 pct   3.4 pct</p>
<p>					 January   December  Year ago</p>
<p> Jobs-to-applicants ratio	 0.76	0.76	0.66</p>
<p> (Unadjusted)			January  December  Year ago</p>
<p> Unemployment rate		  3.3 pct   3.1 pct   3.5 pct</p>
<p> Number of unemployed	     2.22 million  2.08 million  2.30 million</p>
<p> Number of employed		 January    Year/year change</p>
<p> Overall				64.20 million	+1.6 pct</p>
<p>Main Industries:</p>
<p> Manufacturing			14.39 million	+0.9 pct</p>
<p> Services			     16.09 million	+1.1 pct</p>
<p> Wholesale, retail, restaurants 14.64 million	+1.8 pct</p>
<p> Construction			  6.86 million	+6.0 pct</p>
<p> Agriculture			   2.31 million	-8.0 pct</p>
</text>
